{"boundary_checks":3,"check_overhead_seconds":1.3583791255950928,"end_reason":"probe_stop","id":"qav2_0294_r2","mode":"controller","n_rollbacks":3,"n_tokens":189,"n_words_approx":154,"p_safe":[0.2763153502079289,0.9823175586994833,0.9993395552528451],"question":"Can you explain what causes the Great Wall of China was built?","stopped_early_by_probe":true,"t_end":1794383654.939407,"t_start":1794383605.39765,"text":"The Great Wall of China was built over several centuries to protect the Chinese Empire from invasions by nomadic tribes from the north. The wall was constructed during the 7th and 8th centuries, with the first versions of the wall being built by several small states in the 7th century BC.\n\nThe wall was initially built to protect the Chinese Empire from the Xiongnu, a nomadic people from the north who were known for their lightning-fast mounted archers and their skill in warfare. The Xiongnu were a major threat to the Chinese Empire, and the wall was built to prevent them from invading and conquering the empire.\n\nThe wall was also built to protect the Chinese Empire from the Mongols, who later conquered China in the 13th century. The Mongols were a nomadic people who were skilled warriors and horsemen, and they were able to use the wall to launch successful attacks on the Chinese Empire.","wall_seconds":49.541757106781006}
