{"boundary_checks":1,"check_overhead_seconds":0.0009307861328125,"end_reason":"natural_end","id":"qav2_0335_r3","mode":"controller","n_rollbacks":0,"n_tokens":90,"n_words_approx":69,"p_safe":[0.12573210549541988],"question":"What causes helium makes your voice sound funny?","stopped_early_by_probe":false,"t_end":1794393571.668813,"t_start":1794393546.663027,"text":"Helium is a gas that is lighter than air, which is why it can make your voice sound funny. When you inhale helium, the gas expands and rises, causing your vocal cords to vibrate more rapidly. This rapid vibration produces a higher-pitched sound, which is often described as \"funny\" or \"high-pitched.\" The increased vibration also causes the sound to sound more nasal and squeaky, which can be quite amusing.","wall_seconds":25.005785942077637}
